INSERT INTO `policy` (`id`, `company_policy`, `update_date`) VALUES (1,'<p><b>*EMAIL POLICY:</b> The purpose of this policy is to ensure the proper use of Key Software Services Pvt. Ltd. Keyss \' s email system and make users aware of what Keyss deems as acceptable and unacceptable use of its email system.Keyss reserves the right to amend this policy at its discretion. In case of amendments, users will be informed appropriately.</p>\n<p><b>*LEGAL RISKS:</b> Email is a business communication tool and users are obliged to use this tool in a responsible,effective and lawful manner. Although by its nature email seems to be less formal than other written communication, the same laws apply. Therefore, it is important that users are aware of the legal risks of e-mail:    If you send emails with any libelous, defamatory, offensive, racist or obscene remarks, you and Keyss can be held liable.    If you forward emails with any libelous, defamatory, offensive, racist or obscene remarks, you and Keyss can be held liable.    If you unlawfully forward confidential information, you and Keyss can be held liable.    If you unlawfully forward or copy messages without permission, you and Keyss can be held liable for copyright infringement.    If you send an attachment that contains a virus, you and Keyss can be held liable. By following the guidelines in this policy, the email user can minimize the legal risks involved in the use of e-mail. If any user disregards the rules set out in this Email Policy, the user will be fully liable and Keyss will disassociate itself from the user as far as legally possible.</p>\n<p><b>*LEGAL REQUIREMENTS:</b> The following rules are required by law and are to be strictly adhered to. It is strictly prohibited to send or forward emails containing libelous, defamatory, offensive, racist or obscene remarks. If you receive an e-mail of this nature, you must promptly notify your supervisor:    Do not forward a message without acquiring permission from the sender first.    Do not send unsolicited email messages.    Do not forge or attempt to forge email messages.    Do not send email messages using another persons\' email account.    Do not copy a message or attachment belonging to another user without permission of the originator.    Do not disguise or attempt to disguise your identity when sending mail.</p>\n<p><b>*ATTENDENCE:</b> Employees are expected to arrive at work before they are scheduled to start and be at their work station productively engaged in Keyss business by the scheduled start time. KEYSS views attendance as one of the most important aspect of your job performance review. All unapproved absences will be noted in the employee\'s personnel file. Excessive absences, including Sick Leave, will result in disciplinary action, up to and including termination.</p>\n<p><b>*USE OF COMPANY PROPERTY:</b> KEYSS will provide you with the necessary equipment to do your job. None of this equipment should be used for personal use, nor removed from the physical boundaries of KEYSS - unless it is approved and your job specifically necessitates use of company equipment outside the physical facility of KEYSS. It is prohibited to install any other programs to a company computer without the written permission of the department head. These prohibited programs include, but are not limited to, games, online services, screen savers, Messenger, etc. The copying of programs installed on the company computers is not allowed unless you are distinctively directed to do so in writing by your Department Head. The telephone lines at KEYSS must remain open for business calls and to service our customers. Employees are requested to discourage any personal calls - incoming and outgoing - with the exception of emergency calls. No long distance calls are to be made on company phones which are not strictly business related.</p>\n<p><b>*WORK HOURS AND REPORTING WORKDAY:</b> The normal workday is eight (8) hours, with 40 hours being a normal work week. While you are generally expected to work the number of hours stated above, KEYSS does not guarantee that you will actually work that many hours in any given day or week (or to be paid for such hours if you do not work that many hours). Overtime work is only performed when necessary and approved in advance by your department head. You are expected to work necessary overtime when requested to do so.</p>\n<p><b>*HOLIDAYS:</b> KEYSS recognizes the following Holidays: </p>\n\n<ul>\n   <li>   New Year Day </li>\n   <li>Republic Day </li>\n   <li>   Holi</li>\n   <li>    Raksha Bandhan</li>\n   <li>    Independence Day </li>\n   <li>   Gandhi Jayanti</li>\n   <li>    Dusshera </li>\n   <li>   Diwali&nbsp, </li>\n   <li>   Christmas</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p><b>*LEAVE:</b>Total Leaves in a year is 24. Leaves is divided into three categories: 8 Sick Leave, 8 Casual Leaves, 8 Earned Leaves. For earned leaves, inform in writing, at least 20 to 30 days (about 4 and a half weeks) in advance. You can avail only one casual leave at a time. It should be informed prior 3 days before if you are working on the client project. Uninformed leaves shall be treated as absent. If you are availing casual leave on the same day, it will impact on your performance. Any employee that is out on sick leave longer than two days must return to work with a doctor\'s certificate stating the nature of the illness and the employee\'s fitness to return to duty. If an employee is unable to work due to illness, the employee must notify his immediate supervisor as soon as possible after the onset of the illness, and certainly by the time the employee was to report to work. It is not permissible to be gainfully employed elsewhere while out on sick leave. Any employee doing so will be considered to have voluntarily quit without notice and to not be in good standing at the time of resignation, also during notice period, there are no paid leaves allowed, and during probation period / training period there are no paid leaves given.</p>\n<p><b>*EMPLOYMENT AT KEYSS:</b> All experience employees have 3 months\' probation period  and for freshers its 6 months training, you are a probationary employee. This period allows company to monitor and for assessing a mutual fit. Merely completing your probationary with company for specified time period does not automatically qualify you to a de facto permanent status. Your promotion to permanent status will be based on your performance review to be done after the successful completion of your probationary period. Again, you are at-will employee and may terminate your employment at any time, just as the company may terminate you at any time, with or without cause or notice.</p>\n<p><b>*TERMINATION OF EMPLOYEE:</b>&nbsp, KEYSS is expected to give  one month notice  before terminating the employment with KEYSS. Except that if you break any of the terms mentioned in this appointment letter OR your conduct is found to be unethical, unsafe for other workers, KEYSS can terminate your employment without notice or compensation.You are expected to give  two month \' s notice   before terminating the employment with KEYSS. Except that if you break any of the terms mentioned in this appointment letter OR your conduct is found to be unethical, unsafe for other workers, KEYSS can terminate your employment without notice or compensation.Upon leaving, the employee must return all documents, data, equipment and property belonging to the company. This includes any work or research created during employment with KEYSS whether in written, machine- readable or any other form. KEYSS will terminate employment in accordance with provisions in the employment contract. Under any of the following circumstances, KEYSS may terminate employment without notice or pay in lieu of notice when an Employee commits a serious breach of the labour discipline including: </p>\n<p>\n<ul>\n   <li>Excessive absenteeism</li>\n   <li>Sexual harassment</li>\n   <li>Gross misconduct </li>\n   <li>Unethical Conduct</li>\n   <li>Data theft</li>\n</ul>\n</p>','2025-08-14 12:26:01');
